urs when there are unknown issues connecting to a remote host.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass SSLValidationError(ConnectionError):\n    \"\"\"SSLValidationError occurs during a SSL validation failure.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\nYes, I'm fairly confident SSLValidationError subclasses ConnectionError in ansible.module_utils.urls. get_info can confirm.\n\nNow \u2014 the `run` method's `variables` parameter: `self.set_options(var_options=variables, direct=kwargs)`. If I pass `variables=None`, fine.\n\nLet me also think about whether `set_options` might emit warnings or require `self._task`. In `LookupBase.set_options`:\n\n```python\n    def set_options(self, var_options=None, direct=None):\n        super(LookupBase, self).set_options(var_options=var_options, direct=direct)\n\n        # get providers from variables if available, otherwise use self\n        ...\n```\n\nHmm, actually I recall LookupBase.set_options:\n\n```python\n    def set_options(self, var_options=None, direct=None):\n        super(LookupBase, self).set_options(var_options=var_options, direct=direct)\n\n        # get providers from variables if available, otherwise use self\n        self._variable_manager = ...\n```\n\nNo... Let me recall the actual LookupBase:\n\n```python\nclass LookupBase(AnsiblePlugin):\n\n    def __init__(self, loader=None, templar=None, **kwargs):\n\n        self._loader = loader\n        self._templar = templar\n        self._task = None\n        self._host = None\n\n        super(LookupBase, self).__init__(**kwargs)\n\n    def get_basedir(self, variables):\n        ...\n    def _get_deprecated_fqcn_...\n    def set_options(self, var_options=None, direct=None):\n        super(LookupBase, self).set_options(var_options=var_options, direct=direct)\n        # ...\n    def _set_host(...)\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, actually I remember there IS something in LookupBase.set_options about `_templar`:\n\n```python\n    def set_options(self, var_options=None, direct=None):\n        super(LookupBase, sel